      "id": "bc2bogu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Problems of Indian Agriculture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kfkkwy1",
      "content": "• Small land holdings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lu13u15",
      "content": "• Dependence on monsoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g71syee",
      "content": "• Low productivity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "anmwhzq",
      "content": "• Lack of modern technology."
    },
    {
      "id": "l75knt0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Government Initiatives"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Kharif crops (Rice, Maize, Cotton) depend on South-West Monsoon, whereas Rabi crops (Wheat, Mustard) rely on winter rainfall from Western Disturbances.",
        "Dr. M.S. Swaminathan is recognized as the Father of the Green Revolution in India.",
        "Operation Flood relates to Milk production (White Revolution), while Yellow Revolution focuses on Oilseeds.",
        "Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) fixes farmer premium at 2% for Kharif, 1.5% for Rabi, and 5% for commercial crops."
      ],
      "id": "1rtm567"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8y9w977",
      "content": "• Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana – crop insurance scheme."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ufrclat",
      "content": "• Soil Health Card Scheme – improves soil fertility."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jglwzh7",
      "content": "• Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana – irrigation development."
    },
    {
      "id": "qp3ugq0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vm6f9xs",
      "content": "• Kharif crops are sown with the onset of monsoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r5ncs1f",
      "content": "• Punjab and Haryana benefited most from Green Revolution."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8g4rzdm",
      "content": "• Rice is the staple food crop of India."
    }
  ],
